---
import EnglishHeader from './EnglishHeader.astro'; import EnglishFooter from './EnglishFooter.astro'; import OptimizedImage from './OptimizedImage.astro';
import podium from '../assets/stories/jeannie-longo-fransk-mester-2011/jeannie-longo-podium-2011.jpg'; import grenoble from '../assets/stories/jeannie-longo-fransk-mester-2011/jeannie-longo-grenoble-2011.jpg';
const {language='da'}=Astro.props; const en=language==='en'; const base=import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/,''); const slug='jeannie-longo-fransk-mester-2011'; const daUrl=`https://teob.dk/historier/${slug}/`; const enUrl=`https://teob.dk/en/stories/${slug}/`; const canonical=en?enUrl:daUrl; const title=en?'French champion at 52':'Fransk mester som 52-årig'; const description=en?'Jeannie Longo won the 2011 French time trial championship at the age of 52, finishing 42 seconds ahead of the runner-up.':'Jeannie Longo vandt det franske mesterskab i enkeltstart i 2011, 52 år gammel og 42 sekunder foran nummer to.'; const ogImage=new URL(podium.src,canonical).href;
const copy=en?{
 eyebrow:'Women’s cycling · 2011', deck:'Jeannie Longo was older than some of her rivals’ parents. Over 19 kilometres against the clock, she was still the fastest.', lead:'When the clock stopped at 29 minutes and 45 seconds, the 52-year-old had beaten the runner-up by 42 seconds.',
 sections:[['19 kilometres in Boulogne-sur-Mer',['The French time trial championship was held on 23 June 2011. The course around Boulogne-sur-Mer measured 19 kilometres. Longo completed it in 29 minutes and 45 seconds. Christel Ferrier-Bruneau was second, 42 seconds behind. Audrey Cordon finished third.','Her age supplied the headline, but the result sheet offered no masters category in which to hide. Longo won the elite women’s championship. It was her fourth consecutive French time trial title and her eleventh in the discipline.']],['A career across three decades',['Longo had won her first road world championship in 1985. Four more road race world titles followed, along with four individual time trial titles. She won Olympic road race gold in Atlanta in 1996. Those results did not make her any faster in Boulogne-sur-Mer, but they show how long she had been a benchmark in French women’s cycling.','By 2011, 26 years had passed since that first world title. Bicycles, training and the women’s racing calendar had all changed. Longo was still on the start ramp.']]],
 quote:'Fifty-two explained the headline. The 42 seconds explained the win.', endHeading:'The simple measure', end:['A time trial keeps the arithmetic plain. No team-mate can provide a tow and no sprint can conceal the difference. The course and wind are shared. A time stands beside every name.','Longo continued racing after 2011, but this day needs no grand career total to work. She rode the 19 kilometres. The next rider needed another 42 seconds. That settled the title.'], facts:[['52','Jeannie Longo’s age'],['19 km','the time trial distance'],['29:45','the winning time'],['42 sec.','the winning margin']]
}:{
 eyebrow:'Kvindecykling · 2011', deck:'Jeannie Longo var ældre end flere af konkurrenternes forældre. På 19 kilometer mod uret var hun stadig den hurtigste.', lead:'Da tiden stoppede på 29 minutter og 45 sekunder, havde den 52-årige slået nummer to med 42 sekunder.',
 sections:[['19 kilometer i Boulogne-sur-Mer',['Det franske mesterskab i enkeltstart blev kørt den 23. juni 2011. Ruten omkring Boulogne-sur-Mer var 19 kilometer lang. Longo brugte 29 minutter og 45 sekunder. Christel Ferrier-Bruneau blev nummer to, 42 sekunder efter. Audrey Cordon blev nummer tre.','Alderen gav overskrifterne, men resultatlisten havde ingen veteranklasse at gemme sig i. Longo vandt elitekvindernes mesterskab. Det var hendes fjerde franske enkeltstartstitel i træk og den ellevte i disciplinen.']],['En karriere på tværs af tre årtier',['Longo havde vundet sit første VM på landevej i 1985. Senere kom fire yderligere VM-titler i landevejsløbet og fire i enkeltstart. I Atlanta i 1996 vandt hun OL-guld på landevej. Det var ikke meritter, der gjorde hende hurtigere i Boulogne-sur-Mer, men de forklarer, hvor længe hun havde været målestok for fransk kvindecykling.','I 2011 var det 26 år siden det første VM-guld. Cyklerne, træningen og kvindernes løbskalender havde ændret sig. Longo sad stadig på startrampen.']]],
 quote:'52 år forklarede overskriften. De 42 sekunder forklarede sejren.', endHeading:'Den enkle målestok', end:['En enkeltstart gør regnestykket overskueligt. Ingen holdkammerat kan føre, og ingen spurt kan skjule forskellen. Ruten og vinden er fælles. Tiden står ved siden af hvert navn.','Longo fortsatte efter 2011, men denne dag behøver ikke de store karrieretal for at virke. Hun kørte de 19 kilometer. Nummer to brugte 42 sekunder mere. Så var den titel afgjort.'], facts:[['52 år','Jeannie Longos alder'],['19 km','enkeltstartens distance'],['29:45','vindertiden'],['42 sek.','forspringet til nummer to']]
};
